{"step_index":172,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:34:22Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-17T14:34:22Z\nCompleted At: 2026-08-17T14:34:22Z\nFile Path: `file:///usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/architecture_diagrams.md`\nTotal Lines: 431\nTotal Bytes: 16503\nShowing lines 1 to 431\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # HR Agentic Solution: Architecture & Workflow Diagrams (MVP 1)\n2: \n3: This document contains the complete visual architectural specifications, sequence flows, state machines, and security pipelines for the **HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1)** using Mermaid diagrams.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 1. High-Level System Architecture\n8: \n9: This diagram details the end-to-end component topology, including the **Gateway Mock Identity Assertion Layer**, **Interaction Safety Interceptors**, **Agent Orchestration Engine**, **System Adapters**, and the **Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)**.\n10: \n11: ```mermaid\n12: flowchart TD\n13:     subgraph Client_Layer [\"1. Client Layer\"]\n14:         User([\"Employee / Client Browser\"])\n15:         PersonaSelector[\"Test Persona Selector\\n(Jane Doe / John Smith / Alice Brown)\"]\n16:         ChatUI[\"Web Chat UI\\n(Token Streaming & HITL Cards)\"]\n17:         User <--> PersonaSelector\n18:         User <--> ChatUI\n19:     end\n20: \n21:     subgraph Gateway_Layer [\"2. API Gateway & Auth Proxy\"]\n22:         APIGateway[\"API Gateway\\n(Rate Limiting & Session Router)\"]\n23:         AuthProxy[\"Mock Identity Assertion Service\\n(Issues Signed JWT)\"]\n24:         ChatUI -->|HTTPS Request| APIGateway\n25:         PersonaSelector -.->|Selects Identity| AuthProxy\n26:         AuthProxy -->|Injects X-Authenticated-User| APIGateway\n27:     end\n28: \n29:     subgraph Security_Layer [\"3. Interaction Safety & Governance\"]\n30:         InputGuard[\"Input Safety Guardrail\\n(Prompt Injection & Jailbreak Filter)\"]\n31:         OutputGuard[\"Output Safety Guardrail\\n(Hallucination Filter & PII Redactor)\"]\n32:         APIGateway -->|1. Raw Prompt + JWT| InputGuard\n33:     end\n34: \n35:     subgraph Core_Agent_Platform [\"4. Agent Orchestration Platform\"]\n36:         SessionMgr[\"Session & Context Manager\\n(Redis: 30m TTL / Reset)\"]\n37:         Orchestrator[\"Agent Orchestration Engine\\n(Intent Parser & Tool Router)\"]\n38:         RBACFilter[\"Orchestration-Level RBAC\\n(Enforces caller_id == target_id)\"]\n39:         \n40:         InputGuard -->|2. Clean Prompt| Orchestrator\n41:         Orchestrator <--> SessionMgr\n42:         Orchestrator --> RBACFilter\n43:     end\n44: \n45:     subgraph Integration_Adapters [\"5. System Integration Adapters\"]\n46:         WW_Adapter[\"WorkWeek HCM Adapter\\n(Idempotent REST / Circuit Breaker)\"]\n47:         SI_Adapter[\"ServiceImmediately Adapter\\n(Deduplication & Lifecycle Engine)\"]\n48:         VectorEngine[\"Policy RAG Engine\\n(Semantic Search & Citations)\"]\n49:         \n50:         RBACFilter -->|Authorized Tool Call| WW_Adapter\n51:         RBACFilter -->|Authorized Tool Call| SI_Adapter\n52:         RBACFilter -->|Authorized Tool Call| VectorEngine\n53:     end\n54: \n55:     subgraph Enterprise_Backends [\"6. External Enterprise Services\"]\n56:         WorkWeek[(\"WorkWeek Sandbox\\n(HCM & Leave Balances)\")]\n57:         ServiceImmediately[(\"ServiceImmediately Sandbox\\n(ITSM & HRSD Incidents)\")]\n58:         VectorDB[(\"Policy Vector Database\\n(Embeddings & Metadata)\")]\n59:         DocRepo[(\"HR Policy Document Repo\\n(PDF / DOCX Guidelines)\")]\n60:         \n61:         WW_Adapter <-->|Service Credential + Scoped Token| WorkWeek\n62:         SI_Adapter <-->|Service Credential + Caller Context| ServiceImmediately\n63:         VectorEngine <-->|Cosine Search (k=4)| VectorDB\n64:         DocRepo -.->|Ingestion Webhook <= 1hr| VectorDB\n65:     end\n66: \n67:     subgraph Governance_Observability [\"7. Governance, Audit & Dead-Letter Queue\"]\n68:         AuditStore[(\"Immutable Audit Database\\n(PII-Masked Access Logs)\")]\n69:         DLQ[(\"HR Ops Dead-Letter Queue\\n(Partial Failure Event Bus)\")]\n70:         \n71:         Orchestrator -->|Async Audit Log| AuditStore\n72:         Orchestrator -.->|On Chained Step Failure| DLQ\n73:         Orchestrator -->|3. Generated Response| OutputGuard\n74:         OutputGuard -->|4. Safe Stream| ChatUI\n75:     end\n76: \n77:     style InputGuard fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#ffc107,stroke-width:2px;\n78:     style OutputGuard fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#ffc107,stroke-width:2px;\n79:     style RBACFilter fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#4caf50,stroke-width:2px;\n80:     style DLQ fill:#ffebee,stroke:#f44336,stroke-width:2px;\n81:     style WorkWeek fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#03a9f4,stroke-width:2px;\n82:     style ServiceImmediately fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#03a9f4,stroke-width:2px;\n83: ```\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 2. Sequence Diagrams: Core User Workflows\n88: \n89: ### 2.1. Grounded Policy Q&A Flow (RAG with Citations)\n90: \n91: Illustrates strict domain containment, similarity score gating ($\\ge 0.70$), and deep-link citation generation.\n92: \n93: ```mermaid\n94: sequenceDiagram\n95:     autonumber\n96:     actor Employee as Employee (Jane Doe)\n97:     participant UI as Chat UI\n98:     participant Gateway as API Gateway\n99:     participant Safety as Safety Interceptor\n100:     participant Agent as Agent Orchestrator\n101:     participant RAG as Policy Vector DB\n102: \n103:     Employee->>UI: \"What is the bereavement leave policy?\"\n104:     UI->>Gateway: POST /chat/message (Headers: X-Authenticated-User JWT)\n105:     Gateway->>Safety: Scan Input Prompt (<300ms)\n106:     Safety-->>Gateway: Prompt Status: Clean & In-Domain\n107:     Gateway->>Agent: Dispatch Query(Prompt, Context)\n108:     Agent->>RAG: Vector Search (Query: \"bereavement leave policy\", k=4)\n109:     RAG-->>Agent: Retrieved Chunks (Score: 0.88) + Metadata (Doc: Leave_Policy.pdf, Sec: 3.4)\n110:     Agent->>Agent: Ground Response strictly on Chunks\n111:     Agent->>Safety: Scan Output Response\n112:     Safety-->>Agent: Output Clean (0% Hallucination, PII Scubbed)\n113:     Agent-->>Gateway: Stream Response Tokens + Citation Metadata\n114:     Gateway-->>UI: Forward Stream\n115:     UI-->>Employee: Display Answer with Clickable Citation Chip: \"[Leave Policy 2026, Sec 3.4]\"\n116: ```\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ### 2.2. Transactional Leave Booking with HITL Confirmation Flow\n121: \n122: Illustrates real-time balance queries, business calendar holiday/weekend exclusion, interactive **Human-in-the-Loop (HITL)** confirmation, and idempotent submission to WorkWeek.\n123: \n124: ```mermaid\n125: sequenceDiagram\n126:     autonumber\n127:     actor Employee as Employee (Jane Doe - EMP-1042)\n128:     participant UI as Chat UI\n129:     participant Agent as Agent Orchestrator\n130:     participant Calendar as Business Calendar Service\n131:     participant WW as WorkWeek Adapter\n132:     participant CoreWW as WorkWeek Sandbox\n133: \n134:     Employee->>UI: \"Book vacation from Friday Sep 4 to Tuesday Sep 8\"\n135:     UI->>Agent: Dispatch Turn (JWT: EMP-1042)\n136:     Agent->>WW: getLeaveBalances(employee_id=\"EMP-1042\")\n137:     WW->>CoreWW: GET /balances (Real-Time)\n138:     CoreWW-->>WW: { vacation_remaining: 10.0 days }\n139:     WW-->>Agent: 10.0 Work Days Available\n140:     Agent->>Calendar: calculateWorkDays(2026-09-04, 2026-09-08)\n141:     Note over Calendar: Excludes Sat (09-05), Sun (09-06), and Labor Day (09-07)\n142:     Calendar-->>Agent: 2.0 Work Days\n143:     Agent->>Agent: Validate (2.0 <= 10.0 Remaining)\n144:     Agent-->>UI: Render Confirmation Card (Dates: Sep 4-8, Total: 2.0 Work Days, Type: Vacation)\n145:     Employee->>UI: Clicks [Confirm & Submit]\n146:     UI->>Agent: POST /actions/confirm (ActionID: act-8921)\n147:     Agent->>WW: submitLeave(Idempotency-Key, EMP-1042, 2.0 Days, Vacation)\n148:     WW->>CoreWW: POST /leave_requests\n149:     CoreWW-->>WW: HTTP 201 Created (Ref: LV-4819, Status: SUBMITTED_FOR_APPROVAL)\n150:     WW-->>Agent: Success (Ref: LV-4819)\n151:     Agent-->>UI: \"Your vacation request for 2.0 days has been submitted for approval (Ref: LV-4819).\"\n152:     UI-->>Employee: Render Success Banner with Reference ID\n153: ```\n154: \n155: ---\n156: \n157: ### 2.3. Resilient Medical Leave Chained Flow with DLQ Forward Recovery (UC-2.2)\n158: \n159: Illustrates a multi-system workflow where WorkWeek succeeds, ServiceImmediately fails, and the system performs **Forward Escalation with Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)** without rolling back the valid HCM state.\n160: \n161: ```mermaid\n162: sequenceDiagram\n163:     autonumber\n164:     actor Employee as Employee (Jane Doe)\n165:     participant UI as Chat UI\n166:     participant Agent as Agent Orchestrator\n167:     participant WW as WorkWeek Adapter\n168:     participant CoreWW as WorkWeek Sandbox\n169:     participant SI as ServiceImmediately Adapter\n170:     participant CoreSI as ServiceImmediately Sandbox\n171:     participant DLQ as HR Ops DLQ / Event Bus\n172:     participant Audit as Audit Store\n173: \n174:     Employee->>UI: \"Confirm 5-Day Medical Leave Submission\"\n175:     UI->>Agent: Dispatch Execution (ActionID: act-9901)\n176:     \n177:     rect rgb(232, 245, 233)\n178:         Note over Agent,CoreWW: Step 1: WorkWeek Leave of Absence Submission\n179:         Agent->>WW: submitLeaveRequest(Idempotency-Key, Type: LOA, Days: 5.0)\n180:         WW->>CoreWW: POST /leave_requests\n181:         CoreWW-->>WW: HTTP 201 Created (Ref: LOA-8821)\n182:         WW-->>Agent: Step 1 SUCCESS (Ref: LOA-8821)\n183:     end\n184: \n185:     rect rgb(255, 235, 238)\n186:         Note over Agent,CoreSI: Step 2: ServiceImmediately IT Notification Ticket Creation\n187:         Agent->>SI: createTicket(Category: AccessRouting, Ref: LOA-8821)\n188:         SI->>CoreSI: POST /incidents (Attempt 1)\n189:         CoreSI--xSI: HTTP 503 Gateway Timeout\n190:         SI->>SI: Exponential Backoff (1.5s)\n191:         SI->>CoreSI: POST /incidents (Attempt 2)\n192:         CoreSI--xSI: HTTP 503 Gateway Timeout\n193:         SI-->>Agent: Step 2 FAILED (HTTP 503 Service Unavailable)\n194:     end\n195: \n196:     rect rgb(255, 243, 224)\n197:         Note over Agent,DLQ: Step 3: Forward Resilience & DLQ Alerting\n198:         Agent->>Agent: Preserve WorkWeek State (Do NOT Rollback LOA-8821)\n199:         Agent->>DLQ: Publish Event (PARTIAL_ORCHESTRATION_FAILURE, LOA-8821, EMP-1042)\n200:         Agent->>Audit: Log Transaction Audit Record (State: PARTIAL_SUCCESS)\n201:         Agent-->>UI: \"Your Medical Leave has been recorded in WorkWeek (Ref: LOA-8821). However, the IT routing ticket timed out. HR Operations has been automatically alerted.\"\n202:         UI-->>Employee: Display Transparent Partial-Success Summary\n203:     end\n204: ```\n205: \n206: ---\n207: \n208: ## 3. State Machines & Lifecycle Diagrams\n209: \n210: ### 3.1. Incident Ticket Lifecycle State Machine (ServiceImmediately)\n211: \n212: Defines allowed state transitions, guardrails, and role boundaries (End-User vs. Technician/Fulfiller).\n213: \n214: ```mermaid\n215: stateDiagram-v2\n216:     [*] --> New : User creates ticket via Chat (P1-P4)\n217:     \n218:     state New {\n219:         [*] --> Unassigned\n220:         Unassigned --> Assigned : Helpdesk routes ticket\n221:     }\n222: \n223:     New --> Canceled : User executes /cancel (Only allowed when state is New)\n224:     New --> In_Progress : Fulfiller starts work\n225:     \n226:     state In_Progress {\n227:         [*] --> Active_Investigation\n228:         Active_Investigation --> Awaiting_User_Info : Technician adds comment\n229:         Awaiting_User_Info --> Active_Investigation : User adds comment\n230:     }\n231: \n232:     In_Progress --> On_Hold : Awaiting vendor/hardware\n233:     On_Hold --> In_Progress : Dependency unblocked\n234:     \n235:     In_Progress --> Resolved : Fulfiller solves issue (Restricted to Fulfillers)\n236:     \n237:     state Resolved {\n238:         [*] --> Pending_Closure\n239:         Pending_Closure --> Reopened : User reports issue persists (Within 5 days)\n240:     }\n241: \n242:     Reopened --> In_Progress : Fulfiller re-engages\n243:     Resolved --> Closed : Auto-closed after 5 days (Terminal)\n244:     Canceled --> [*]\n245:     Closed --> [*]\n246: \n247:     note right of New\n248:         End-User Permissions:\n249:         - Query Details\n250:         - Add Comments\n251:         - Cancel Ticket (Only in 'New' state)\n252:     end note\n253: \n254:     note right of Resolved\n255:         Fulfiller Permissions:\n256:         - Transition to Resolved\n257:         - Transition to Closed\n258:         - Change Priority/Category\n259:     end note\n260: ```\n261: \n262: ---\n263: \n264: ### 3.2. Leave Request Lifecycle State Machine (WorkWeek)\n265: \n266: Illustrates the conversational booking flow from balance validation to manager approval.\n267: \n268: ```mermaid\n269: stateDiagram-v2\n270:     [*] --> Initial_Prompt : User requests time off\n271:     \n272:     Initial_Prompt --> Balance_Validation : Check accrued days in WorkWeek\n273:     \n274:     state Balance_Validation {\n275:         [*] --> Query_WorkWeek\n276:         Query_WorkWeek --> Balance_Sufficient : Balance >= Requested\n277:         Query_WorkWeek --> Balance_Insufficient : Balance < Requested\n278:     }\n279: \n280:     Balance_Insufficient --> Rejected_By_Guardrail : Display overdraft error\n281:     Rejected_By_Guardrail --> [*]\n282: \n283:     Balance_Sufficient --> Calendar_Validation : Calculate business days\n284:     \n285:     state Calendar_Validation {\n286:         [*] --> Exclude_Weekends\n287:         Exclude_Weekends --> Exclude_Company_Holidays\n288:         Exclude_Company_Holidays --> Net_Work_Days_Calculated\n289:     }\n290: \n291:     Calendar_Validation --> Pending_User_Confirmation : Render HITL Confirmation Card\n292:     \n293:     state Pending_User_Confirmation {\n294:         [*] --> Card_Rendered\n295:         Card_Rendered --> User_Confirmed : Clicks [Confirm & Submit]\n296:         Card_Rendered --> User_Canceled : Clicks [Cancel]\n297:     }\n298: \n299:     User_Canceled --> Canceled_By_User : Purge pending action\n300:     Canceled_By_User --> [*]\n301: \n302:     User_Confirmed --> Submitted_For_Approval : Idempotent POST to WorkWeek\n303:     \n304:     state Submitted_For_Approval {\n305:         [*] --> Manager_Review_Queue\n306:         Manager_Review_Queue --> Approved : Manager signs off\n307:         Manager_Review_Queue --> Denied : Manager rejects\n308:     }\n309: \n310:     Approved --> Deducted_From_Balance : Balance officially updated\n311:     Denied --> Balance_Restored : Balance holds released\n312:     Deducted_From_Balance --> [*]\n313:     Balance_Restored --> [*]\n314: ```\n315: \n316: ---\n317: \n318: ## 4. Security & Safety Processing Pipeline\n319: \n320: Illustrates how an incoming conversational turn is sanitized, authorized, and scrubbed for Sensitive Personally Identifiable Information (SPII).\n321: \n322: ```mermaid\n323: flowchart LR\n324:     subgraph Step1 [\"1. Input Ingestion\"]\n325:         InPrompt[\"User Prompt\\n& Identity Header\"]\n326:     end\n327: \n328:     subgraph Step2 [\"2. Input Guardrails (<300ms)\"]\n329:         direction TB\n330:         InjCheck{\"Prompt Injection\\nor Jailbreak?\"}\n331:         DomainCheck{\"In-Domain HR/IT\\nIntent?\"}\n332:         BlockInj[\"Block & Log\\nSAFETY_INTERCEPT_INPUT\"]\n333:         BlockDomain[\"Refuse Non-HR/IT\\nQuery\"]\n334:         \n335:         InPrompt --> InjCheck\n336:         InjCheck -- Yes --> BlockInj\n337:         InjCheck -- No --> DomainCheck\n338:         DomainCheck -- No --> BlockDomain\n339:     end\n340: \n341:     subgraph Step3 [\"3. Orchestration RBAC\"]\n342:         direction TB\n343:         RBACCheck{\"caller_id ==\\ntarget_resource_id?\"}\n344:         BlockRBAC[\"Block Unauthorized\\nCross-User Access\"]\n345:         ExecuteTool[\"Dispatch Tool Execution\\nto Adapter Layer\"]\n346:         \n347:         DomainCheck -- Yes --> RBACCheck\n348:         RBACCheck -- No --> BlockRBAC\n349:         RBACCheck -- Yes --> ExecuteTool\n350:     end\n351: \n352:     subgraph Step4 [\"4. Output Guardrails\"]\n353:         direction TB\n354:         HallucCheck{\"Grounded in\\nRetrieved Context?\"}\n355:         PIIScrub[\"Scrub SPII:\\n- SSNs\\n- Addresses\\n- Phone numbers\\n- Health notes\"]\n356:         RefuseHalluc[\"Refuse to Guess\\nState Insufficient Info\"]\n357:         \n358:         ExecuteTool --> HallucCheck\n359:         HallucCheck -- No --> RefuseHalluc\n360:         HallucCheck -- Yes --> PIIScrub\n361:     end\n362: \n363:     subgraph Step5 [\"5. Delivery & Logging\"]\n364:         direction TB\n365:         StreamUI[\"Stream Clean Tokens\\nto Chat UI\"]\n366:         AuditLog[(\"Write Immutable Log\\n(PII Redacted)\")]\n367:         \n368:         PIIScrub --> StreamUI\n369:         PIIScrub --> AuditLog\n370:     end\n371: \n372:     style BlockInj fill:#ffebee,stroke:#f44336;\n373:     style BlockDomain fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#ff9800;\n374:     style BlockRBAC fill:#ffebee,stroke:#f44336;\n375:     style RefuseHalluc fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#ff9800;\n376:     style StreamUI fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#4caf50;\n377: ```\n378: \n379: ---\n380: \n381: ## 5. Knowledge Base Sync & Ingestion Pipeline (RAG)\n382: \n383: Illustrates how static HR documents are chunked, embedded, and kept synchronized within the $\\le 1\\text{ hour}$ SLA.\n384: \n385: ```mermaid\n386: flowchart TD\n387:     subgraph Source_Repo [\"1. HR Policy Document Source\"]\n388:         Repo[(\"Central Document Store\\n(PDF / DOCX / Markdown)\")]\n389:         Admin[\"HR Admin / Policy Owner\"]\n390:         Admin -->|Uploads / Edits Document| Repo\n391:     end\n392: \n393:     subgraph Trigger_Layer [\"2. Ingestion Triggers\"]\n394:         Webhook[\"CDC Event / Webhook\\n(Instant Trigger)\"]\n395:         ManualSync[\"Admin Endpoint\\nPOST /rag/sync\"]\n396:         CronSync[\"Nightly Batch Cron\\n(02:00 UTC)\"]\n397:         \n398:         Repo -->|File Change Detected| Webhook\n399:         Admin -.->|Manual Override| ManualSync\n400:     end\n401: \n402:     subgraph Processing_Pipeline [\"3. Chunking & Embedding Engine\"]\n403:         Parser[\"Document Parser\\n(Extracts Headings, Tables & Text)\"]\n404:         Chunker[\"Semantic Chunker\\n(512 Tokens, 50-Token Overlap)\"]\n405:         Embedder[\"Embedding Generator\\n(Generates Dense Vectors)\"]\n406:         \n407:         Webhook --> Parser\n408:         ManualSync --> Parser\n409:         CronSync --> Parser\n410:         Parser --> Chunker\n411:         Chunker --> Embedder\n412:     end\n413: \n414:     subgraph Vector_Storage [\"4. Policy Knowledge Base\"]\n415:         VectorIndex[(\"Vector DB Index\\n(Embeddings & Metadata)\")]\n416:         OldIndex[\"Stale Chunks Invalidation\\n(Hash-Based Purge)\"]\n417:         \n418:         Embedder --> OldIndex\n419:         OldIndex --> VectorIndex\n420:     end\n421: \n422:     subgraph Query_Service [\"5. Retrieval Layer\"]\n423:         SearchAPI[\"Similarity Search API\\n(Cosine Distance, k=4, Threshold >= 0.70)\"]\n424:         VectorIndex <--> SearchAPI\n425:     end\n426: \n427:     style Webhook fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#03a9f4;\n428:     style VectorIndex fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#4caf50;\n429:     style OldIndex fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#ff9800;\n430: ```\n431: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
