FR-1.5, FR-3.1), the solution uses an API Gateway Mock Identity Assertion Layer (injecting signed JWT `X-Authenticated-User` headers from a Chat UI test persona switcher).\n- **Cross-System Failure Handling**: SAGA 2-phase rollback is too complex and risky for MVP 1 (WorkWeek leave could already be locked). The agreed resolution is **Forward Escalation with Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)**: retain successful WorkWeek state, emit a high-priority alert to the HR Ops DLQ, and give the employee a partial-success summary with their reference ID.\n- **gdocs CLI Command Quirks**:\n  - `gdocs mutate replace` without `--direct` creates native Google Docs suggestions / tracked changes.\n  - `gdocs mutate replace` with `--direct` applies edits directly without suggestion markup.\n  - `gdocs mutate add-comment` supports `--native` and `--quote` for inline text anchoring.\n  - `gdocs mutate reply-comment` takes `docID`, `commentID`, and reply text.\n  - `gdocs mutate format-named-styles` with `--preset bluedoc` applies Google Sans styling.\n  - `write_to_file` requires all user-facing and temporary artifact files to reside in `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n#### Edited / Created Artifact Files\n- `/usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/architecture_diagrams.md`: Full visual architecture, C4 container diagram, sequence flows (RAG, Leave booking HITL, Medical leave DLQ), state machines (Incident lifecycle, Leave lifecycle), security guardrail pipeline, and RAG ingestion sync pipeline.\n- `/usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/specs_and_user_stories.md`: Top-level functional specifications, API contracts, and Agile user stories with Gherkin acceptance criteria across 6 Epics.\n- `/usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/scratch/brd_v2.md`: Clean markdown baseline of revised BRD.\n- `/usr