{"step_index":184,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:36:32Z","content":"You can open and preview the markdown artifacts directly using the links below:\n\n---\n\n### 📊 **1. Architecture & Workflow Diagrams (Mermaid)**\nClick to open in Markdown Preview:  \n👉 **[architecture_diagrams.md](file:///usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/architecture_diagrams.md)**\n\n**Contains:**\n* 🏗️ **High-Level System Topology:** Complete C4-style diagram spanning Client UI, API Gateway & Auth Proxy, Safety Interceptor, Agent Orchestration Engine, Adapters, Vector DB, and Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ).\n* 🔄 **Core Sequence Diagrams:**\n  * Grounded Policy Q&A with deep-link citation chips.\n  * Self-Service Leave Booking with business calendar exclusions and **Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) Confirmation Cards**.\n  * Chained Medical Leave flow with partial failure handling and **DLQ alert dispatching**.\n* ⚙️ **State Machines:** ServiceImmediately Incident lifecycle & WorkWeek Leave Request lifecycle.\n* 🛡️ **Safety & RBAC Pipeline:** 5-stage input/output sanitization, JWT identity extraction, and PII masking.\n* 📚 **RAG Knowledge Base Sync Pipeline:** Webhook/CDC ingestion, semantic chunking, and embedding refresh.\n\n---\n\n### 📋 **2. Functional Specifications & User Stories**\nClick to open in Markdown Preview:  \n👉 **[specs_and_user_stories.md](file:///usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/specs_and_user_stories.md)**\n\n**Contains:**\n* 🎯 **16 Detailed User Stories across 6 Epics** with priority, story points, and technical schemas.\n* 🧪 **Gherkin Acceptance Criteria (`Given-When-Then`)** for all core flows and failure edge cases.\n* 📜 **Data Contracts:** `X-Authenticated-User` signed JWT format, API error envelopes, and `Idempotency-Key` headers."}
